## 6298-6350 · 2026-09-28 · Paseo #5410: PI/V2 mechanism resolved; v1-specific scope confirmed
The #5410 investigation concluded: PI's `transformContext` modifies only the input `AgentMessage[]` (Pi restores original state after the handler returns), so PI has no stored-message rewrite → no #5410 trigger. The user corrected the bug's framing: it's the model's habit of emitting N markers into literal text, and MC's V1 plugin strips them from the stored output (downstream cleanup). On PI, MC strips them from the input context (upstream prevention). The user challenged the "no mechanism" claim for PI, leading to verification via the PI `ContextEvent` doc and MC issue #70. Recorded the v1/v2/PI mechanism comparison in the research doc (commit 02d64a3). Then verified the V2 conclusion via MC issue #492: V2's context hook has message access (`SessionContext.messages: V2Message[]`) but the messages are a `ReadonlyArray` copy — V2 rewrites the input draft, not the store. Corrected the research doc (commit 3abe0e7). Final scope: V1 fixed (PR #5558, a4618c5), V2 and PI no fix needed (both input-only). Docker test beds torn down.

## 6351-6391 · 2026-09-28 · Paseo #5410: MC-side fix investigated and rejected; text.complete hook identified as actual trigger
Investigated whether #5410 could be fixed on the MC side. Found that MC's v1 code already uses `experimental.chat.messages.transform` (input-only, in-place splice) for tag prevention — contradicting the prior assumption that MC uses a persisted `context` hook. The actual #5410 trigger is MC's `experimental.text.complete` hook (`text-complete.ts`), which strips N noise from assistant text via `stripPersistedAssistantText` and persists via `session.updatePart`. The MC-side fix (disabling `text.complete`) is not viable because the `messages.transform` prevention doesn't work — the model still emits N tags (the context is full of them), so the cleanup is necessary and inherently produces the non-extending update. The Paseo-side fix (PR #5558) is the complete and correct solution. User noted the MC path might be broken due to an API bug discussed earlier.

## 6392-6452 · 2026-09-28 · Paseo #5410: N-marker mechanism resolved; PI persisted strip found, V1-specific scope confirmed
The #5410 investigation resolved the N-marker mechanism and scope. Verified the #25754 API bug is NOT the cause — MC's messages.transform uses in-place splice correctly, and N markers are intentionally in the input context (for ctx_reduce). The #5410 bug is inherent to MC's design. The user provided the key evidence (PI's strip-tag-prefix.ts GitHub link) showing PI has a persisted strip that mirrors text-complete.ts. This corrected the scope to V1 + PI. Then, after examining the PI implementation in detail, the scope was corrected back to V1-specific: the PI stripping hook mutates the stored message at message_end but does NOT emit a new text_delta event, so the Paseo PI provider never sees the stripped text → no #5410 bug on PI (just cosmetic &lt;tag&gt; tags). V2 has zero  handling. Final scope: V1 only (fixed in PR #5558).

## 6453-6460 · 2026-09-28 · Paseo #5410: PI pre-persistence strip confirmed; text-change event question opened
The #5410 PI investigation confirmed the MC stripping is a **pre-persistence** mutation (at `message_end`, before the jsonl write), correcting an earlier imprecision. The PI runtime has no post-persistence modification event — the Paseo PI provider only sees the `&lt;tag&gt;`-tagged `text_delta` events from generation, never the stripped text. The user raised an open question: PI might have a text-change event for user-facing reconciliation (a mechanism that can remove a whole message while showing full output should have user-facing implementation). The user corrected the search scope to the PI runtime (pi-coding-agent) as the source of truth, not Paseo. Chunk ends mid-investigation of the PI runtime's event flow.

## 6461-6501 · 2026-09-28 · Paseo #5410: PI fix identified and implemented (message_end replace)
The PI runtime emits a `message_end` event carrying the **stripped** text (after MC's stripping hook mutates text parts at `message_end`, before `sessionManager.appendMessage` persists). The Paseo PI provider's `handleMessageEnd` was ignoring this event — just clearing `activeAssistantMessageId`. The fix: emit the `message_end` text as a `replace: true` item (same shape as the V1 fix in PR #5558). Implemented in the Paseo clone (`handleMessageEnd` + `extractAssistantText` helper + `PiAssistantContent`/`PiTextContent` imports). 180 PI provider tests pass, typecheck clean. Research doc corrected to V1+PI scope (commits cba0993, 52e137e; V1 fix at a4618c5).

