## 7455-7569 · 2026-09-29 · Shared-stealth-browser MCP/supervisor debugging: playwright-core packaging, esbuild crash, SingletonLock
Debugged the shared-stealth-browser MCP/supervisor/browser launch. The core issue: esbuild bundling marks `playwright-core` as external, but the runtime directory doesn't have `node_modules` with it (unlike the original `agent-browser` which was self-contained). Fixed by shipping `node_modules` in the runtime directory (matching the original's pattern, confirmed via Paseo plugin docs). The MCP server then crashed with `Class2 is not a constructor` (esbuild bundling issue); after fixes, MCP connects and ticket validation passes. The MCP tools are for interacting with a running browser, not starting it — the browser is started by the plugin's `handleAttachBrowser` RPC when the UI panel is opened (by design in the original). Chromium leaves `SingletonLock` behind on crash, blocking relaunch; the code doesn't clean it up. The UI shows "shared-browser" (old ID) due to a cache issue; the real bug is the missing SingletonLock cleanup.

