## 7783-7835 · Shared-stealth-browser CDP input frame-staleness fix
Fixed the CDP input frame-staleness bug in shared-stealth-browser that was blocking the avito search. The supervisor's frame validation was too aggressive: it compared full state (including the `controllerExpiresAt` timestamp) instead of just the navigation generation, so dynamic page elements (popup, auto-refresh) and the slow local 27B model's capture→input gap kept invalidating the frame. A subagent fixed two bugs: frame TTL raised from 5s to 300s (the 27B model's round-trip exceeded 5s), and the `bridgeEpoch` check removed (any re-bridge invalidated the frame). The staleness check now compares `navigationGeneration` only. 53/53 tests pass. After a supervisor restart, input (click/type) works; the avito search field is clickable and typable.

## 7836-7901 · 2026-09-30 · Shared-stealth-browser interaction fixes: lease, frame persistence, naming, drag interpolation, beginFrame streaming
Fixed four interaction issues in shared-stealth-browser via subagents: control lease raised from 30s to 5min with auto-renew; frame validation relaxed so a captured frame survives input ops (only invalidated by navigation/viewport/control transfer); MCP tool names renamed from `shared_browser_*` to bare action names; drag events interpolated into 24 lerp steps at 16ms. The user then reported that during a drag, the screencast produces no intermediate frames because CDP screencast is compositor-driven (only produces frames when the page re-renders). After researching via the browser per the user's directive, found `HeadlessExperimental.beginFrame` — the only Chrome mechanism for compositor-level frame scheduling, exclusive to chrome-headless-shell. Implemented a 30fps beginFrame pump with 9 Chrome args, in-flight guard, and screencast lifecycle integration. 59/59 tests pass.

## 7902-7959 · 2026-09-30 · Shared-stealth-browser: beginFrame rejected for interactive drag, CSS frame pump implemented
The beginFrame pump (HeadlessExperimental.beginFrame with --enable-begin-frame-control) was rejected for interactive drag: deterministic mode only produces frames on explicit request, so frames stop during a drag. Replaced with a CSS frame pump — a 30fps opacity animation injected via CDP Runtime.evaluate that forces continuous compositor frames without changing the rendering model. 61/61 tests pass. Plugin enable/disable lifecycle used for restarts instead of manual process killing. Documented in playwright-mcp.md + README.md, commit 2c90bd1.

