## 9633-9641 · 2026-10-20→21 · Evaluated Terraphim AI against maxima stack — skip verdict
U: take a look at this instead https://terraphim.ai

Fetched and analyzed Terraphim AI (Alex Mikhalev, Apache-2.0, v1.21.22, Rust+WASM): a local-first knowledge-graph search engine using Aho-Corasick automata + a built-in English thesaurus for concept-based retrieval, ships an MCP server, role-based KGs, multi-source indexing including session-history search. Evaluated against our stack: zvec-grep (semantic), CodeGraph (symbols), MC ctx_search (FTS+archive). ~70% overlap with what we already run.

U: well, session searching is not what i'm interested in, it claims to create easy to search knowledge base, like let's say if we pull a lot of docs for a project, like cuda once, it would provide index which pulls exactly what you need in a moment instead of requiring you to grep folder and then do positional or full file reads

Reframed the evaluation to the "docs corpus → instant precise retrieval" lane. The CUDA-corpus comparison is the strongest baseline: cuda-skill already implements that pattern (preprocessed corpora + query scripts). Terraphim's English thesaurus is structurally weak on PTX/NCCL jargon — its headline feature (synonym expansion) contributes nothing on our vocabulary. Deterministic explainability is the counter-design to embedding search but our corpora need semantic recall more than term adjacency.

U: so generally speaking it's no better than maxima-data-analysis stack, even worse at some part

Agreed — maxima pattern (pull → insert → SQLite FTS5 → precise query) gives the same guarantee with composable retrieval (SQL joins, snippet(), auditable BM25). Terraphim gives opaque ranking; a SQL table is a schema you own. Their index is their format; the SQLite file is the durable artifact per the script-is-the-engine doctrine. One portable idea: the role-KG as a per-domain synonym dictionary table for FTS5 query expansion (half a day, attacks vocabulary mismatch).

U: well i'm honestly like those stack and maybe it's worth to be turned into some kind of app, yet since i use it trough opencode i just don't have to to get value from current shape

Confirmed: the app layer exists for humans without agent workflows — route the substrate through an agent and the UI is absorbed. The corpus+index+scripts pattern is the durable asset; whoever builds the app is building our UI for us.

